 <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What is an IP address?</h3><p>It's a unique number that identifies a device on a network so data can be routed to it. Your device uses one to communicate over the internet or a local network.</p><h3>What's the difference between public and private IP?</h3><p>Your public IP is the address websites and the internet see (assigned to your router); your private IP identifies your device within your own home or office network.</p><h3>What is the difference between IPv4 and IPv6?</h3><p>IPv4 uses 32-bit addresses (like 192.168.1.1) and is running out; IPv6 uses 128-bit addresses to provide vastly more, supporting the growing number of devices.</p><h3>How do I find my IP address?</h3><p>Search 'what is my IP' to see your public IP. Your private IP appears in your device's network settings.</p><h3>Does a VPN change my IP address?</h3><p>Yes. A VPN routes your traffic through another server, so websites see that server's IP instead of your real public IP, adding privacy.</p><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@graph": [{"@type": "BlogPosting", "headline": "What Is My IP Address? A Beginner's Guide (2026)", "about": "what is my ip address", "url": "https://studenttimepk.blogspot.com/2026/07/what-is-my-ip-address-complete.html", "dateModified": "2026-09-15", "author": {"@type": "Organization", "name": "Students Time"}, "publisher": {"@type": "Organization", "name": "Students Time"}}, {"@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "What is an IP address?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "It's a unique number that identifies a device on a network so data can be routed to it. Your device uses one to communicate over the internet or a local network."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What's the difference between public and private IP?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Your public IP is the address websites and the internet see (assigned to your router); your private IP identifies your device within your own home or office network."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What is the difference between IPv4 and IPv6?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "IPv4 uses 32-bit addresses (like 192.168.1.1) and is running out; IPv6 uses 128-bit addresses to provide vastly more, supporting the growing number of devices."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How do I find my IP address?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Search 'what is my IP' to see your public IP. Your private IP appears in your device's network settings."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Does a VPN change my IP address?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. A VPN routes your traffic through another server, so websites see that server's IP instead of your real public IP, adding privacy."}}]}]}</script><!--related-guides-->
